  "why": "The paper does not design its failure oracle, mutation, or exploration specifically to discover or bypass model safeguards (e.g., adversarial training, input detectors, or safety-aligned models), nor does it empirically demonstrate bypassing such safeguards. DeepHunter uses a metamorphic oracle (human-semantics preservation) and coverage-guided seed/mutation strategies to find prediction errors and to detect quantization-induced inconsistencies, but the authors never describe using or attacking defenses nor using feedback from safeguards to guide fuzzing. The experimental evaluations focus on coverage, error quantity/diversity, and quantization errors, not on bypassing adversarially-trained or detector-protected models.",
